-- statement:
--   **Cost of the rotation descriptor for `n`.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFMSE`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFM.descTrP_cost_n (dst rw rm : Fin HS) (hd : TrOk dst rw rm) {n : ℕ} (hn : IntMul.OpenAI.Glue.n0 ≤ n)
--       (w m : ℕ) (hwA : w ≤ 2 ^ (2 * bP n + 2)) (hmA : m ≤ 2 ^ (2 * bP n + 2)) (t : IState HS)
--       (h : TrRegs t n w m rw rm) :
--       (descTrP dst rw rm).cost t ≤ 10 ^ 12 * (bP n + 1) ^ 3
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFM SE: the axis-rotation descriptor (`TransNeed`)*: `descTr w h bs = [w, h, k, b_0, …, b_{k−1}]` (KFMNeed). In kmain the array has the padded shape
--   `[t_0, …, t_{d−1}]` (`t_j = 2^{h + b_j}`, `h = ℓ − 1`, `b_j = [d' ≤ j]`). After `m` rotations
--   its shape is that list rotated left by `m`, so the descriptor of the next rotation uses the bits
--   `bR n m j = [d' ≤ (j + m) mod d]`.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** This lemma belongs to layer 5 of the Lean formalization (integer-multiplication-kappa campaign) of the OpenAI preprint *Integer multiplication below $n\log n$*: the uniform item-language machine (register programs over the `NLogN` multitape framework) assembling the Proposition 14 / Lemma 13 / Proposition 18 pieces, the resampling and chirp stages and the cost recurrences into one fixed machine, culminating in `NLogN.KFTop.kappa_bound : IntMul.KappaBound (1 / 2 ^ 182)` (the bound of `Def_IntMul_MultitapeModel`). All names refer to the definition bundles up to `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs33`.
